{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition","kind":"proposition","title":"Decomposition quantity $c_5^{\\mathrm{dec}} = -b^2 - 1/2 = -3/2 + 1/[2]_q^2$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-silver-ratio-beta-decay-null"],"cites":["references/wenzl1988","references/hoefsmit1974","references/jones1985"],"tags":["lean-infrastructure","c5-outlier","involution-operator","averaged-crossing","bar-invariance","leibniz-propagation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_decomposition_via_quantum_two","text":"c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.md","leanSource":"c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition\"></a><p><em>For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\neq 0</code> define the Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling squared on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2,1)}</code>,</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">b(q)^2 \\;=\\; \\frac{q^4+q^2+1}{(q^2+1)^2},</code></pre>\n<p><em>and the decomposition quantity</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">c_5^{\\mathrm{dec}}(q) \\;:=\\; \\underbrace{-b(q)^2}_{\\text{pure-}\\sigma\\text{ Kashiwara}} \\;-\\; \\underbrace{\\tfrac{1}{2}}_{\\text{averaged-crossing fingerprint}} .</code></pre>\n<p><em>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b(q)^2 = 1 - 1/[2]_q^2</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q + q^{-1}</code>, and hence</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">c_5^{\\mathrm{dec}}(q) \\;=\\; -\\tfrac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{[2]_q^{2}} .</code></pre>\n<p><em>This statement does not identify <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_5^{\\mathrm{dec}}</code> with the rung-5 coefficient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_5</code> of the <a href=\"#prop:q-beta-categorical-precision-ladder\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta</code> categorical-derivation precision ladder</a>; that identification is a separate, unproved claim, and the ladder itself requires re-derivation at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code>. At the silver ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1+\\sqrt2</code> the pure-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code> part evaluates to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-b^2 = -7/8</code> (<a href=\"#prop:silver-ratio-beta-decay-null\"><strong>Silver-ratio trace degeneracy</strong></a>).</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"21.2.2","page":"b/prop-c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":95,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":89},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.c5_decomposition_via_quantum_two","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
